// Monitor surface: FrameCounter (completed 02 frames), DumpFrame "path" (P6 PPM, nibble * 17),
// GetFramebufferBase64, GetFramebufferRowHex y, GetPixel x y, GetJournal / JournalCount /
// ClearJournal, PixelsStored (pixels stored by all 02 frames), FaultWrongId.
.
4,8c
//   - 0x02 SPI cache write: 02, A23-A16, A15-A8, A7-A0, one dummy byte (0xFF), then 4-bpp pixels,
//     two per byte, the high nibble first (MSB-first SPI clocks it first). Address = {5'b0, ROW[8:0],
//     COL[9:0]} in PIXELS, so any column (odd too) can start a write. A pixel is stored only once 4
//     more SCLK cycles follow it in the same CS frame ("Final 4 dummy clocks are needed", datasheet
//     7.3.15): a frame with n data bytes stores 2n - 1 pixels and its last nibble only supplies the
//     dummy clocks. Measured on the arm (0.3.8, virtual-display.md 6): w/2 pixel bytes + a trailing
//     0 byte store w + 1 pixels, the extra one a 0 at the next address.
//     The address advances one pixel at a time and wraps from column 639 to column 0 of the next row
//     (datasheet 4.2.2, also measured). Writes past (639, 479) are dropped (assumption; not measured).
//   - 0x03 SPI cache read: 03, A23-A16, A15-A8, A7-A0, one dummy byte, then the cache from that
//     pixel address, two pixels per byte, high nibble first, with the same wrap; FillByte past the end.
//   - 0x9F: identification (ID 0x4010 on the bytes after IdReadLatency dummies).
//   - other known opcodes: journaled, no side effects (current, luminance, offsets, 97 Sync...).
//     The cache -> pixel latch at 0x97 is not modelled: pixels land in the image at once.
.
